  "toyota_summary": "A major European automaker announced plans to cut as many as 8,000 jobs by the end of 2027, with severance packages beginning in October. The cuts come as the company grapples with slowing demand and the costly shift to electric vehicles. This is the largest single reduction at the company in years.\n\nFor the industry, this signals that margin pressure is real and immediate. Companies are no longer waiting to see if demand recovers—they're restructuring now. Expect more announcements from competitors facing similar headwinds in Europe and China.\n\nWatch whether other manufacturers follow suit in the coming weeks, and whether unions accept the proposed packages without significant disruption.",
